      {
        "id": 2658573447,
        "content": "Too lazy to block quote all this o1 pro response from mobile:\nYou can do it using the repository invitation endpoints rather than the org membership endpoints. Specifically:\n\t1.\tInvite the bot as a collaborator:\nPOST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/collaborators/{username}\n\t2.\tAs the bot, fetch pending repository invites:\nGET /user/repository_invitations\n\t3.\tAccept any new invitation:\nPATCH /user/repository_invitations/{invitation_id}\nThis avoids switching to an org. Store a PAT for the “ubiquity-os-simulant” bot in your Cloudflare Worker and use the above flow.\n[GitHub docs reference.](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/collaborators/collaborators#accept-a-repository-invitation)",
